      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm stuck on my lit review. if i have a source with 5 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for APA 7th edition? also how is that different from how i'd do it in chicago style? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In the APA 7th edition, when you have a source with 5 authors, you would list all five authors the first time you cite the source in your text. After that, you can use the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" (and) and the year of publication. For example, (Smith, Johnson, Williams, Brown, Davis, 2020). In subsequent citations, you would use (Smith et al., 2020).\n\nIn Chicago style, you would list all five authors the first time you cite the source in your text. After that, you can use the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" (and) and the year of publication. For example, Smith et al. (2020).\n\nSo, in both styles, you would list all five authors the first time you cite the source, but after that, you would use the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" (and) and the year of publication. The main difference is in the formatting of the in-text citation, with APA using parentheses and Chicago using commas.",
